        <h2>Safari Planning Tips</h2>
        <p><strong>Book jeeps in advance</strong> between November and April (peak season) — jeeps at popular parks like Yala sell out by the night before. Walk-up morning availability is unreliable in high season. The best approach is to book a package that includes accommodation and the jeep together, as lodge guesthouses manage their own jeep allocation.</p>
        <p><strong>Arrive before dawn.</strong> The gate opens at 5:30am. The first two hours of daylight are when predators are active, birds are calling and light is best for photography. Arriving at 7am means the best is already over — the animals that were on the move at 5:30am are now resting in shade.</p>
        <p><strong>Expect crowds at Yala</strong> during school holiday periods. In January and August, Block 1 can have 200+ jeeps chasing the same leopard sighting. Wilpattu avoids this entirely; Udawalawe is less crowded than Yala but still busy in peak season.</p>
        <p><strong>Combine parks efficiently.</strong> Yala + Udawalawe + Bundala can be covered in 3 days based from Tissamaharama. Wilpattu pairs naturally with Anuradhapura (2 days). Minneriya sits in the Cultural Triangle. Sinharaja is a day trip from Ratnapura.</p>

